sequenceDiagram
    %% Flow 1: Training Job Lifecycle
    rect rgb(240, 248, 255)
        Note over User,HeadlessSvc: Flow 1: Training Job Lifecycle
        participant User as User / SDK
        participant K8sAPI as Kubernetes API Server<br/>443/TCP HTTPS TLS 1.2+
        participant Webhook as Training Operator Webhook<br/>9443/TCP HTTPS TLS 1.2+
        participant Controller as Training Operator Controller
        participant Pods as Training Pods<br/>(replicas)
        participant HeadlessSvc as Headless Services<br/>(inter-replica DNS)

        User->>K8sAPI: Create *Job CR (e.g. PyTorchJob)<br/>Auth: Bearer Token / kubeconfig
        K8sAPI->>Webhook: POST /validate-kubeflow-org-v1-*job<br/>Auth: API server mTLS
        Webhook-->>K8sAPI: Admission Response (allow/deny)
        K8sAPI-->>User: CR created / rejected

        Note over Controller: Reconciliation loop triggered
        Controller->>K8sAPI: Create Pods (per replica spec)<br/>Auth: ServiceAccount token
        K8sAPI-->>Controller: Pod status updates (informer watch)
        Controller->>K8sAPI: Create Headless Service<br/>Auth: ServiceAccount token
        Controller->>K8sAPI: Update *Job status<br/>Auth: ServiceAccount token

        Pods->>Pods: Inter-replica communication<br/>via headless service DNS<br/>TCP (user-defined ports)
    end

    %% Flow 2: PyTorch Elastic Training
    rect rgb(255, 248, 240)
        Note over Controller,Pods: Flow 2: PyTorch Elastic Training

        participant HPA as HorizontalPodAutoscaler

        Controller->>K8sAPI: Create HPA for PyTorchJob<br/>Auth: ServiceAccount token
        Note over HPA: HPA scales worker replicas

        participant MasterPod as Master Pod<br/>(rendezvous server)
        participant WorkerPods as Worker Pods

        WorkerPods->>MasterPod: Rendezvous registration<br/>RDZVPort/TCP
        WorkerPods->>WorkerPods: Distributed training<br/>via headless service DNS<br/>TCP (user-defined ports)
    end

    %% Flow 3: MPI Job Execution
    rect rgb(240, 255, 240)
        Note over Controller,WorkerPodsMPI: Flow 3: MPI Job Execution

        participant LauncherPod as Launcher Pod
        participant WorkerPodsMPI as Worker Pods (MPI)

        Controller->>K8sAPI: Create ConfigMap (hostfile, kubexec.sh)<br/>Auth: ServiceAccount token
        Controller->>K8sAPI: Create ServiceAccount + Role + RoleBinding<br/>Auth: ServiceAccount token
        Controller->>K8sAPI: Create Launcher + Worker Pods<br/>Auth: ServiceAccount token

        LauncherPod->>K8sAPI: pods/exec into Workers<br/>443/TCP HTTPS TLS 1.2+<br/>Auth: ServiceAccount RBAC
        K8sAPI-->>WorkerPodsMPI: kubectl exec session
        LauncherPod->>WorkerPodsMPI: MPI commands via kubexec.sh
    end
